{"strongs": "H0251", "word": "אָח", "translit": "ach", "root": "אחה", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "brother", "definition": "I. אָח 630 noun masculine brother (Phoenician אח , Arabic (construct etc.), Sabean אחֿ (suffix אחֿיהו ) CIS iv.1,17 and 24 and others, Ethiopic Assyrian a—u compare Dl W , Aramaic אַח , ; Palmyreme, Nabataean suffix אחוהי , אחיה ); — absolute אָח Gen 24:29 + ( Ezek 18:10 strike out Co compare ᵐ5 ᵑ6 ᵑ9 ; Ew Sm אַח ; Dl Ba Ez x defends as = one compare Assyrian a—u ) never with article; cstr אֲחִי Gen 10:21 +; suffix אָחִי Gen 4:9 +; אָחִיךָ Gen 4:9 +; אָחִיו Gen 4:2 +; אָחִיהוּ Jer 34:9 + 3 t. etc.; plural אַחִים Gen 13:8 +; so read Hos 13:15 see De Compl. Var. 23 compare below אָחוּ ; construct אֲחֵי Num 27:10 +; suffix אַחַי Gen 19:7 +; אֶחָ֑י 1Sam 20:29 + (but 1Sam 30:23 ᵐ5 We אַחֲרֵי for אֶחָ֑י את ); אַחֶיךָ Gen 37:13 +; אֶחָיו Gen 44:14 + etc. 1. brother , born of same mother (& father) Gen 4:2 ; Gen 4:8 ; Gen 4:9 ; Gen 4:10 ; Gen 4:11 ; Gen 27:6 ; Gen 27:11 ; Gen 44:20 ; Gen 49:5 compare Gen 28:2 ; Gen 29:10 (twice in verse) + Exod 4:14 + often; also of half-brother Gen 20:5 ; Gen 20:13 ; Gen 20:16 (on pa-rentage compare v Gen 20:12 ) Gen 37:2 ; Gen 37:4 ; Gen 37:5 +, 2Sam 13:4 ; 2Sam 13:7 ; 2Sam 13:8 +. 2. indefinite = relative; Lot, of Abraham Gen 13:8 ; Gen 14:12 ; Gen 14:14 ; Gen 14:16 Jacob, of Laban Gen 29:12 ; Gen 29:15 (nephew); hence of kinship in wider sense; member of same tribe Num 16:10 ; Num 18:2 ; Num 18:6 ; 2Sam 19:13 of same people Exod 2:11 (twice in verse); Exod 4:18 ; Deut 15:12 ; Judg 14:3 ; Isa 66:20 ; Neh 5:1 ; Neh 5:5 ; Neh 5:8 see especially Lev 19:17 compare v Lev 19:18 (ex-tended to include sojourner גֵּר v Lev 19:34 ); of Israel & Judah 2Sam 19:42 Israel & Edom Num 20:14 compare of Ishmael Gen 16:12 ; Gen 25:18 of friend 2Sam 1:26 ; 1Kgs 9:13 ; 1Kgs 20:32 ; 1Kgs 20:33 of allies ׳ בְּרִית א Amos 1:9 . 3. figurative of resemblance Job 30:29 אָח הָיִיתִי לְתַנִּים (|| רֵעַ לִבְנוֺת יַעֲנָה i.e. by reason of his crying, compare Di ; Prov 18:9 מִתְרַפֶּה בִּמְלַאכְתּוֺ אָח הוּא לְבַעַל מַשְׁחִית . 4. in phrase one . . . another אִישׁ אָחִיו Gen 9:5 ; Joel 2:8 Ze Joel 7:10 אִישׁ ֗֗֗ אָחִיו Gen 13:11 + 25 t + Exod 32:27 (where also same phrase with רֵעֵהוּ & קְרֹבוֺ — see these words — & also אִישׁ , אֶחָד ; for development of idiom compare Deut 15:2 ; Isa 19:2 ; Jer 34:14 (compare15) 17 Ezek 38:21 ; Hag 2:22 usually of men; of faces of golden cherubim Exod 25:20 ; Exod 37:9 of scales of crocodile Job 41:9 . ( אָח fire-pot . see below II. אחח .)", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB285')\">BDB285</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H251')\">H251</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB284')\">BDB284</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB286')\">BDB286</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>אָח</bdbheb><sub>630</sub> <b>noun masculine</b> <highlightword>brother</highlightword> (Phoenician <bdbheb>אח</bdbheb>, Arabic <placeholder136/> (construct <placeholder137/> etc.), Sabean <bdbheb>אחֿ</bdbheb> (suffix <bdbheb>אחֿיהו</bdbheb>) <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('CIS')\">CIS<sup>iv.1,17 and 24</sup></lookup> and others, Ethiopic <placeholder138/> Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>a—u</highlight></transliteration> compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>W</sup></lookup>, Aramaic <bdbarc>אַח</bdbarc>, <placeholder139/>; Palmyreme, Nabataean suffix <bdbheb>אחוהי</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אחיה</bdbheb>); — absolute <bdbheb>אָח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 24:29\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(1,24,29)\">Gen 24:29</ref> + (<ref ref=\"Ezek 18:10\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(26,18,10)\">Ezek 18:10</ref> strike out <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Co')\">Co</lookup> compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Syr')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ6</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick